    65	## 3. Architecture
    66	
    67	### 3.1 T1: ledger plus idiomatic entity projection
    68	
    69	The ledger stays the canonical record: exact values, both clocks, assertion identity, retractions,
    70	receipts, journal and claims. Each engine adds a projection in its own idiom, derived from a
    71	release-bound projection spec (EntityTypes and attributes mapped to physical names and declared types).
    72	One engine-neutral planner (`planProjection`, EXP-R01) computes projection changes for both lanes so
    73	their semantics cannot drift. The hook point is each adapter's `persist()` (R9), which already receives
    74	every row of the transaction.
    75	
    76	```
    77	                          Triplex TypeScript API
    78	   +------------------------------------------------------------------+
    79	   | Repository<Model>: at(basis) get getMany find timeline            |
    80	   | Writer -> WritePlan -> commit(plans, {actor, commandId})          |
    81	   | native.xtql`` native.sql`` native.sparql`` + declared contract    |
    82	   +-----------------+--------------------------------+---------------+
    83	                     | eligibility check (C1)          |
    84	        eligible     v                                 v   not eligible
    85	   +----------------------------------+  +-------------------------------+
    86	   | ENTITY PROJECTION                |  | EXACT LEDGER PATH             |
    87	   | XTDB: table per type, _id =      |  | same native language, closed  |
    88	   |  entity id, ns$attr columns,     |  | basis relations over the      |
    89	   |  native valid time; index tables |  | ledger (facts, history,       |
    90	   |  keyed by value (hypothesis)     |  | values)                       |
    91	   | QLever: current graph of plain   |  |                               |
    92	   |  typed triples + publication     |  |                               |
    93	   |  marker                          |  |                               |
    94	   +----------------------------------+  +-------------------------------+
    95	        XTDB: ledger + projection in one engine transaction.
    96	        QLever: log decision, then one update operation per commit group (C2).
    97	```
