   290	## 7. The evolutionary loop
   291	
   292	### 7.1 One generation
   293	
   294	```
   295	   +-------------+     +-------------+     +----------------+     +-------------+
   296	   | 1 read      | --> | 2 select    | --> | 3 brief and    | --> | 4 agents    |
   297	   | STATE,      |     | by dep graph|     | dispatch       |     | build and   |
   298	   | SCORECARD,  |     | + progress  |     | (<=10 agents,  |     | run gates   |
   299	   | NOTEBOOK,   |     | obligations,|     |  atomic pool)  |     | in own      |
   300	   | acceptance  |     | 2-3 rivals  |     |                |     | worktrees   |
   301	   +-------------+     +-------------+     +----------------+     +------+------+
   302	         ^                                                               |
   303	   +-----+-------+     +-------------+     +----------------+            |
   304	   | 7 next      | <-- | 6 select:   | <-- | 5 independent  | <----------+
   305	   | generation  |     | promote on  |     | verifier on    |
   306	   |             |     | frozen      |     | the integrated |
   307	   |             |     | budgets     |     | candidate      |
   308	   +-------------+     +-------------+     +----------------+
   309	```
   310	
   311	1. **Read state:** `lab/STATE.md`, `lab/SCORECARD.md`, the notebook tail, and obligation status computed from
   312	   `lab/acceptance/obligations.json` and receipts.
   313	2. **Select by dependency graph.** Every OPEN obligation has an experiment within three generations; an
   314	   obligation with no progress for two generations escalates (new research, engine repair, or a design
   315	   change); at most two unintegrated branches per lane; two or three rivals per measured bottleneck.
   316	3. **Brief and dispatch** with the template in 7.3.
   317	4. **Build and run** in the agent's own worktree on `exp/<id>-<slug>`, gates through `lab/bin`.
   318	5. **Verify** on the integrated candidate (main plus the branch), by an agent that did not write it.
   319	6. **Promote** only when hard semantic invariants hold (binary, never traded) and the integrated candidate's
   320	   cumulative cost stays inside the frozen profile budgets (7.4). Losers stay in the notebook with the reason.
   321	7. **Next generation:** mutate winners, combine partial winners, retire hypotheses that failed twice for the
   322	   same reason. A failed falsifier blocks its dependents until a new design passes it.
   323	
   324	**Hourly learnings pass.** A session cron (job `ae766d26`, hourly at :07) updates the notebook from finished
   325	experiments and launches Sonnet research where the learnings raise a question the next generation needs answered.
   326	
   327	### 7.2 Agent roles
   328	
   329	| Role | Model and effort | Job |
   330	| --- | --- | --- |
   331	| Research | Sonnet, xhigh | go wide on the web and in pinned source, probe engines, write `lab/research/*.md` |
   332	| Coding | Opus, high | one experiment per agent from a commander's-intent brief |
   333	| Verifier | Opus, high | rerun gates on the integrated candidate, try to break the claim |
   334	| Adversarial review | Codex `gpt-6.1-sol`, xhigh | plans, contracts, gate or oracle changes, major promotions |
